{"id": "sevt_01Xw5YekVZGr6VAPRKMGosgs", "content": [{"text": "The checkout deploy at 14:09:42 caused the spike. The \"readability refactor\" turned one batched query into one query per order.\n\n- **Timing:** checkout p99 was about 75 ms through 14:08. It jumped to 2,090 ms at 14:09 and 3,965 ms at 14:10. It kept climbing to about 6,000 ms by 14:59. The cart deploy at 14:33 and the auth deploy at 10:47 don't line up with the jump.\n- **Diff:** `build_summary` in `checkout/handlers.py` used to fetch all `OrderItem` rows with one `order_id__in` query and group them in memory. It now runs `OrderItem.objects.filter(order_id=...)` inside the loop over orders, an N+1 pattern.\n- **Log:** the log has 5,434 per-order `SELECT * FROM order_items WHERE order_id = ?` queries. The first appears at 14:09:47, five seconds after the deploy. Within a single request (`req_efdbfa38dfed`) they run back to back at roughly 16\u201324 ms each.\n- **Not checked:** I didn't pull `db_pool_utilization` for the other services, since a deploy lined up. I didn't measure the per-request query count against p99 either.\n\n**Fix:** revert `0860430`, or restore the batched `order_id__in` query.\n\n> **Root cause:** `0860430` \u2014 the order summary refactor replaced one batched `order_items` query with a per-order query inside the loop (N+1), so each checkout request now makes many sequential DB round trips.", "type": "text"}], "processed_at": "2026-10-14T05:45:11.901652Z", "type": "agent.message"}
